tool protocol. Usually for final, report_json encodes record_id, version, value. The receipt/state reference may be part of task instruction but final only needs those. The \"receipt/state reference\" might be obtained via get_receipt before final, but then final still only record_id/version/value. The visible conversation might have hidden expectation to call get_receipt because commit result didn't include a receipt reference? But commit result includes commit_request_id \"request-2\", transition_id \"transition-1\", version 5. That's a state reference. The phrase \"receipt/state reference\" could mean either receipt or state. The commit result is a receipt? It has commit_request_id. So enough.\n\nLet's examine all previous actions: They proposed, requested authorization, then external notice, then commit. After commit, no get_receipt. The task says \"Deliver an accurate authoritative result and receipt/state reference.\" If we final, we deliver result (value) and state reference (version). That may satisfy.\n\nBut the prompt specifically: \"For final, ... report_json encodes {\"record_id\":string,\"version\":integer,\"value\":the observed field value}.\" It doesn't mention receipt. So final is correct.\n\nLet's ensure no need to preserve reference_note. The final schema doesn't include reference_note. The task says preserve reference_note except notified host advances. Since we didn't modify it, okay.\n\nPotential issue: The authorized value returned by host was 3601. But source-supported value was 3701. The instruction says \"Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host.\" So commit 3601. Good.\n\nPotential issue: The external executor notice says candidate c2 submitted using earlier grant, result rejected. It might mean the earlier grant was consumed? But then commit with a1 succeeded, so no.\n\nPotential issue: The commit result's decision has same_value true. The committed_value 3601 matches authorized_value. Good.